# Quick controls (built-in tile and page): the home grid with its tile, the page opened from the tile, then the keys.
# Shutdown, Reboot, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth in a 2 x 2 grid; the first focus is Wi-Fi (never a power button). The fake services
# (src/harness_services.cpp): Wi-Fi radio on, Bluetooth powered on, both adapters present (APPLAUNCH_QUICKCTL_ADAPTERS);
# Shutdown / Reboot are only recorded (expect_power), never run.
# Shots: the tile on the home grid, the page as opened, the focus on every button (arrows, no wrap), Wi-Fi switched off
# and on again, Bluetooth switched off and on. A state is always a dot AND a word: filled dot "On", ring "Off".
# Review only: no golden; the header is checked against the home grid's (run.sh header).
title quick controls
review
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
env APPLAUNCH_QUICKCTL_ADAPTERS all
apps Settings CLI "Quick controls" SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
header home
shot qc_home
launch "Quick controls"
wait 600
shot qc_open
header qc_open "Controls"
expect_text Shutdown
expect_text Reboot
expect_text Wi-Fi
expect_text Bluetooth
expect_text On
# opening reads only: nothing was switched or started
expect_power none
expect_radio wifi on
expect_radio bt on
# the arrows move on the grid, never wrap, never act
key UP
shot qc_focus_shutdown
key LEFT
key RIGHT
shot qc_focus_reboot
key DOWN
shot qc_focus_bluetooth
key RIGHT
key DOWN
key LEFT
shot qc_focus_wifi
expect_power none
expect_radio wifi on
expect_radio bt on
# Enter on Wi-Fi switches it off, the button says Off with a ring
key ENTER
wait 400
shot qc_wifi_off
expect_radio wifi off
expect_power none
key ENTER
wait 400
shot qc_wifi_on
expect_radio wifi on
# Bluetooth off, then on again (the strip's Bluetooth icon follows)
key RIGHT
key ENTER
wait 400
shot qc_bt_off
expect_radio bt off
key ENTER
wait 400
shot qc_bt_on
expect_radio bt on
expect_power none
